---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

/**
 * Teaching toy: two optimization models linked through a surrogate (Jones,
 * 2026-10-11). The model is src/scripts/surrogateLinkModel.js, with tests
 * beside it. Every number is illustrative and made up for this page; nothing
 * comes from a paper, a proposal or a real plant. The page names no proposal
 * and no review status, and credits the surrogate-optimization line it builds
 * on (UTA's COSMOS center).
 *
 * Its companion is "What a Grid Is Made Of", where the reader picks the mix.
 * Here a model picks it, and the question is whether the next model can trust
 * a cheap stand-in for the first.
 */
---

<Base title="Accurate, and Still Wrong" wide={true} og="models"
      description="A teaching toy: a surrogate can predict one model's output well and still send the next model to the wrong decision.">
  <p class="subhead">Two optimization models, linked through a cheap stand-in for the first. The stand-in fits well and still sends the second model the wrong way.</p>

  <p class="disclaimer">
    <strong>This is a teaching toy, not research.</strong> Both models are
    tiny, every number is made up for this page, and none of it describes a
    real grid, plant or supply chain. No number it produces should be cited.
    It exists to make one mechanism visible.
  </p>

  <h2>The setup</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>planning model</strong> picks the cheapest way to meet a fixed
    demand for power from four candidate plans, from solar with storage to all
    gas. Solar panels and batteries need far more metal than gas plants, so as
    the price of materials rises the cheapest plan jumps from one to the next.
    The metal the chosen plan needs is handed to a <strong>supply-chain
    model</strong>, which picks which of three processing plants to open to
    supply it.
  </p>
  <p>
    In real studies the planning model takes hours to run, so it is run a
    handful of times and a <strong>surrogate</strong> (here a Gaussian process,
    fitted by maximum likelihood) is trained on those runs to predict its output
    at any price. The supply-chain model then plans on the surrogate's
    prediction instead of the real thing.
  </p>

  <div class="model" id="link">
    <div class="controls">
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Runs of the planning model</legend>
        <label>Spread over the price range <output data-for="n"></output>
          <input type="range" id="n" min="4" max="16" step="1" value="8">
        </label>
        <div class="actions stack">
          <button type="button" id="add" class="reset">Add a run where it is least certain</button>
          <button type="button" id="resample" class="reset">Resample</button>
        </div>
        <p class="hint" id="runs-hint"></p>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend>Look at one price</legend>
        <label>Material price index <output data-for="p"></output>
          <input type="range" id="p" min="0.5" max="2.5" step="0.01" value="1">
        </label>
        <p class="hint">1.0 is today's price in this toy.</p>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="button" id="reset" class="reset">Reset</button>
        <button type="button" id="share" class="reset">Copy link</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="output">
      <svg id="chart" viewBox="0 0 720 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="chart-title chart-desc">
        <title id="chart-title">Metal the planning model's plan needs, against material price: the true staircase and the surrogate's smooth fit</title>
        <desc id="chart-desc"></desc>
      </svg>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i class="sw sw-true"></i>Planning model (true)</span>
        <span><i class="sw sw-gp"></i>Surrogate's prediction</span>
        <span><i class="sw sw-band"></i>Surrogate's uncertainty (±2σ)</span>
        <span><i class="sw sw-run"></i>A run of the planning model</span>
        <span><i class="sw sw-wrong"></i>Wrong plants opened</span>
      </div>

      <svg id="strip" viewBox="0 0 720 96" role="img" aria-labelledby="strip-title">
        <title id="strip-title">Which processing plants the supply-chain model opens at each price: planning on the true model, and planning on the surrogate</title>
      </svg>
      <p class="hint">Plants: A large refinery (500 kt), B mid-size plant (300 kt), C small plant (200 kt). Darker means more capacity opened.</p>

      <dl class="readout" id="here"></dl>
      <dl class="readout" id="overall"></dl>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>What this is showing</h2>
  <p>
    The black line is a staircase because a planning model's answer does not
    slide; it jumps between a few corner solutions as the price moves. The
    surrogate is smooth. With eight runs it explains most of the variation and
    looks like a good fit. But each step's flat top sits just above or below a
    point where the supply-chain model needs another plant, so a prediction off
    by a few percent lands on the wrong side and opens the wrong plants. The red
    bands are those prices. Where the plan comes up short, the metal has to be
    bought in a hurry at a premium.
  </p>
  <p>
    Try it: add runs and watch the fit improve faster than the decisions do.
    Resample and see how much depends on where the runs happened to land. Then
    move the price into a red band and read the cost of acting on the
    surrogate.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it matters</h2>
  <p>
    Linking models is how one study's output becomes another's input: a grid
    plan becomes a materials forecast, which becomes a supply chain. When the
    first model is too slow to run everywhere, a surrogate stands in for it.
    This toy's lesson is that the usual test of a surrogate, how well it
    predicts, is the wrong test when its prediction feeds a decision. What
    matters is whether the next model makes the same choice it would have made
    with the real thing: the same plants, the same binding limits, a plan that
    can actually be carried out. Judging a surrogate on the decision, and
    choosing where to run the expensive model by what it does to the decision,
    is open research.
  </p>

  <h2>What it leaves out</h2>
  <p>
    Nearly everything that makes real linked models hard. One input instead of
    dozens; four candidate plans instead of a continuous build-out; three plants
    and no geography, transport or time. Real planning models are linear or
    mixed-integer programs with thousands of variables, and real supply-chain
    models have many tiers. The surrogate here is a textbook Gaussian process on
    a one-dimensional Latin hypercube; the "add a run" button uses the textbook
    rule of sampling where the surrogate is least certain.
  </p>
  <p class="hint">
    The approach builds on the design and analysis of computer experiments
    (DACE) and surrogate-optimization work of UT Arlington's COSMOS center
    (V. Chen, J. Rosenberger and colleagues). Model:
    <code>src/scripts/surrogateLinkModel.js</code>, with its tests beside it, no
    dependencies. Companion toy: <a href="/materials/">What a Grid Is Made Of</a>,
    where you choose the mix instead of a model.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .disclaimer {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: .6rem .9rem;
    background: var(--code-bg);
    font-size: .92rem;
  }
  .model { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 15rem 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .model { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .controls fieldset {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px;
    padding: .6rem .8rem .8rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem;
  }
  .controls legend {
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--accent); padding: 0 .3rem;
  }
  .controls label {
    display: block; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: .82rem;
    color: var(--muted); margin-top: .5rem;
  }
  .controls input[type=range] { width: 100%; margin-top: .2rem; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .controls output { float: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--text); }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: .4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .actions.stack { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; margin-top: .6rem; }
  .reset {
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: .8rem; background: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; padding: .3rem .7rem;
    color: var(--muted); cursor: pointer; text-align: center;
  }
  .reset:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text); }
  .hint { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .5rem 0 0; }
  #chart, #strip { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  #strip { margin-top: .8rem; }
  .legend {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .2rem 1rem;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .4rem;
  }
  .sw { display: inline-block; width: .9rem; height: .7rem; margin-right: .3rem; vertical-align: -1px; border-radius: 2px; }
  .sw-true { background: var(--text); height: .16rem; border-radius: 0; vertical-align: 3px; }
  .sw-gp { background: var(--accent); height: .2rem; border-radius: 0; vertical-align: 3px; }
  .sw-band { background: var(--accent); opacity: .18; }
  .sw-run { width: .6rem; height: .6rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); }
  .sw-wrong { background: var(--wrong); opacity: .25; }
  .model { --wrong: #b23a2e; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .model { --wrong: #f07a6e; } }
</style>

<style is:global>
  /* Readout cells are built by the script, so these must be global; held under #link. */
  #link .readout {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
    gap: .6rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  #link .readout div { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; padding: .5rem .7rem; }
  #link .readout div.bad { border-color: var(--wrong); }
  #link .readout dt { font-size: .72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: var(--muted); }
  #link .readout dd { margin: .15rem 0 0; font-size: 1.15rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  #link .readout dd small { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>

<script>
  import {
    PRICE, PROCESSORS, upstreamBreaks, latinHypercube, evaluate, nextRun, operate, downstream,
  } from "../scripts/surrogateLinkModel.js";

  const root = document.getElementById("link");
  const $ = (s) => root.querySelector(s);
  const NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
  const el = (name, attrs = {}, text) => {
    const n = document.createElementNS(NS, name);
    for (const k in attrs) n.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);
    if (text != null) n.textContent = text;
    return n;
  };
  const clear = (svg) => { while (svg.childNodes.length) {
    const last = svg.lastChild;
    if (last.nodeName === "title" || last.nodeName === "desc") break;
    svg.removeChild(last);
  } };

  const DEFAULT = { n: 8, seed: 1, extra: [], p: 1 };
  const state = { ...DEFAULT, extra: [] };
  const BREAKS = upstreamBreaks();
  // Darker = more capacity opened.
  const SETS = ["C", "B", "BC", "A", "AC", "AB", "ABC"];
  const shade = (k) => 0.18 + 0.72 * (SETS.indexOf(k) / (SETS.length - 1));
  const plants = (k) => k.split("").join("+");

  let ev = null;
  function recompute() {
    const xs = [...latinHypercube(state.n, state.seed), ...state.extra];
    ev = evaluate(xs);
  }

  // ------------------------------------------------------------ main chart
  function drawChart() {
    const svg = $("#chart");
    clear(svg);
    const W = 720, H = 340, L = 56, R = 12, T = 30, B = 34;
    const yMax = 1000;
    const x = (p) => L + ((p - PRICE.min) / (PRICE.max - PRICE.min)) * (W - L - R);
    const y = (v) => H - B - (Math.max(0, Math.min(yMax, v)) / yMax) * (H - T - B);
    const rows = ev.rows;
    const dx = (rows[1].p - rows[0].p) / 2;

    // Wrong-decision bands, behind everything.
    for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; ) {
      if (rows[i].chosen === rows[i].truth) { i++; continue; }
      let j = i;
      while (j + 1 < rows.length && rows[j + 1].chosen !== rows[j + 1].truth) j++;
      svg.appendChild(el("rect", {
        x: x(rows[i].p - dx), y: T, width: x(rows[j].p + dx) - x(rows[i].p - dx), height: H - T - B,
        fill: "var(--wrong)", opacity: .13,
      }));
      i = j + 1;
    }

    for (let v = 0; v <= yMax; v += 200) {
      svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1: L, x2: W - R, y1: y(v), y2: y(v), stroke: "var(--rule)", "stroke-width": 1 }));
      svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: L - 8, y: y(v) + 4, "text-anchor": "end", "font-size": 11, fill: "var(--muted)",
        "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, v));
    }
    svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: L - 8, y: T - 12, "text-anchor": "end", "font-size": 10, fill: "var(--muted)",
      "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, "kt of metal"));
    for (let p = 0.5; p <= 2.501; p += 0.5) {
      svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: x(p), y: H - B + 16, "text-anchor": "middle", "font-size": 11, fill: "var(--muted)",
        "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, p.toFixed(1)));
    }
    svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: (L + W - R) / 2, y: H - 4, "text-anchor": "middle", "font-size": 11,
      fill: "var(--muted)", "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, "material price index"));

    // Regime boundaries and the plan chosen in each.
    const edges = [PRICE.min, ...BREAKS.map((b) => b.p), PRICE.max];
    const mixes = [BREAKS[0].from, ...BREAKS.map((b) => b.to)];
    BREAKS.forEach((b) => svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1: x(b.p), x2: x(b.p), y1: T - 4, y2: H - B,
      stroke: "var(--muted)", "stroke-width": 1, "stroke-dasharray": "3 3" })));
    mixes.forEach((m, i) => svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: (x(edges[i]) + x(edges[i + 1])) / 2, y: T - 12,
      "text-anchor": "middle", "font-size": 10.5, fill: "var(--text)", "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, m.label)));

    // Uncertainty band.
    let band = `M ${x(rows[0].p)} ${y(rows[0].Dhat + 2 * rows[0].sd)}`;
    for (const r of rows) band += ` L ${x(r.p)} ${y(r.Dhat + 2 * r.sd)}`;
    for (let i = rows.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) band += ` L ${x(rows[i].p)} ${y(rows[i].Dhat - 2 * rows[i].sd)}`;
    svg.appendChild(el("path", { d: band + " Z", fill: "var(--accent)", opacity: .15 }));

    // True staircase.
    let st = `M ${x(rows[0].p)} ${y(rows[0].D)}`;
    for (let i = 1; i < rows.length; i++) st += ` L ${x(rows[i].p)} ${y(rows[i - 1].D)} L ${x(rows[i].p)} ${y(rows[i].D)}`;
    svg.appendChild(el("path", { d: st, fill: "none", stroke: "var(--text)", "stroke-width": 2 }));

    // Surrogate mean.
    let gp = `M ${x(rows[0].p)} ${y(rows[0].Dhat)}`;
    for (const r of rows) gp += ` L ${x(r.p)} ${y(r.Dhat)}`;
    svg.appendChild(el("path", { d: gp, fill: "none", stroke: "var(--accent)", "stroke-width": 2.2 }));

    // Runs.
    ev.xs.forEach((p, i) => svg.appendChild(el("circle", { cx: x(p), cy: y(ev.ys[i]), r: 4.5,
      fill: "var(--accent)", stroke: "var(--bg)", "stroke-width": 1.5 })));

    // The price being inspected.
    svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1: x(state.p), x2: x(state.p), y1: T, y2: H - B,
      stroke: "var(--text)", "stroke-width": 1.2, opacity: .7 }));
  }

  // ----------------------------------------------------------- decision strip
  function drawStrip() {
    const svg = $("#strip");
    clear(svg);
    const W = 720, L = 56, R = 12, rowH = 30;
    const x = (p) => L + ((p - PRICE.min) / (PRICE.max - PRICE.min)) * (W - L - R);
    const rows = ev.rows;
    const dx = (rows[1].p - rows[0].p) / 2;
    const lanes = [["True plan", "truth", 8], ["Surrogate", "chosen", 52]];
    for (const [label, key, top] of lanes) {
      svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: L - 6, y: top + rowH / 2 + 4, "text-anchor": "end", "font-size": 10.5,
        fill: "var(--muted)", "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, label));
      for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; ) {
        let j = i;
        while (j + 1 < rows.length && rows[j + 1][key] === rows[i][key]) j++;
        const x0 = x(rows[i].p - dx), x1 = x(rows[j].p + dx);
        svg.appendChild(el("rect", { x: x0, y: top, width: Math.max(0.5, x1 - x0), height: rowH,
          fill: "var(--accent)", "fill-opacity": shade(rows[i][key]) }));
        if (x1 - x0 > 30) {
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x: (x0 + x1) / 2, y: top + rowH / 2 + 4, "text-anchor": "middle",
            "font-size": 10.5, "font-weight": 600, fill: "var(--text)",
            "font-family": "system-ui, sans-serif" }, plants(rows[i][key])));
        }
        i = j + 1;
      }
    }
    // Outline the surrogate's wrong stretches.
    for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; ) {
      if (rows[i].chosen === rows[i].truth) { i++; continue; }
      let j = i;
      while (j + 1 < rows.length && rows[j + 1].chosen !== rows[j + 1].truth) j++;
      svg.appendChild(el("rect", { x: x(rows[i].p - dx), y: 52, width: x(rows[j].p + dx) - x(rows[i].p - dx),
        height: rowH, fill: "none", stroke: "var(--wrong)", "stroke-width": 2 }));
      i = j + 1;
    }
    svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1: x(state.p), x2: x(state.p), y1: 4, y2: 86,
      stroke: "var(--text)", "stroke-width": 1.2, opacity: .7 }));
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- readouts
  function cells(dl, items) {
    dl.innerHTML = "";
    for (const [k, v, sub, bad] of items) {
      const d = document.createElement("div");
      if (bad) d.className = "bad";
      const dt = document.createElement("dt"); dt.textContent = k;
      const dd = document.createElement("dd"); dd.textContent = v;
      if (sub) { const s = document.createElement("small"); s.textContent = ` ${sub}`; dd.appendChild(s); }
      d.append(dt, dd); dl.appendChild(d);
    }
  }

  function readouts() {
    const rows = ev.rows;
    const r = rows.reduce((b, q) => (Math.abs(q.p - state.p) < Math.abs(b.p - state.p) ? q : b), rows[0]);
    const wrong = r.chosen !== r.truth;
    const ran = operate(downstream(Math.max(0.01, r.Dhat)).open, r.D);
    cells($("#here"), [
      ["Metal needed", `${Math.round(r.D)} kt`, r.mix.label],
      ["Surrogate says", `${Math.round(r.Dhat)} kt`, `±${Math.round(2 * r.sd)}`],
      ["Plants, true plan", plants(r.truth)],
      ["Plants, surrogate", plants(r.chosen), wrong ? "wrong" : "same", wrong],
      ["Cost of trusting it", r.regret < 0.05 ? "none" : `+${r.regret.toFixed(1)}`,
        ran.short > 0 ? `short ${Math.round(ran.short)} kt` : (wrong ? "overbuilt" : ""), wrong],
    ]);
    const s = ev.summary;
    cells($("#overall"), [
      ["Runs used", String(ev.xs.length)],
      ["Fit across prices", `R² ${s.r2.toFixed(2)}`, `error ${s.maePct.toFixed(0)}% of range`],
      ["Wrong plants at", `${Math.round(s.wrongPct)}%`, "of prices", s.wrongPct > 0.5],
      ["Short of metal at", `${Math.round(s.shortPct)}%`, "of prices", s.shortPct > 0.5],
    ]);
    $("#runs-hint").textContent = state.extra.length
      ? `${state.n} spread evenly at random, plus ${state.extra.length} added where the surrogate was least certain.`
      : `Spread by a Latin hypercube: one at random in each of ${state.n} equal slices of the price range.`;
    $("#chart-desc").textContent = `With ${ev.xs.length} runs the surrogate's fit has R squared ${s.r2.toFixed(2)}, `
      + `yet the supply-chain model opens the wrong plants at ${Math.round(s.wrongPct)} percent of prices.`;
  }

  function labels() {
    root.querySelector('output[data-for="n"]').textContent = String(state.n);
    root.querySelector('output[data-for="p"]').textContent = state.p.toFixed(2);
  }

  // ----------------------------------------------------------- share state
  function readShare() {
    const q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    const num = (k, lo, hi) => { const v = Number(q.get(k)); return q.has(k) && Number.isFinite(v) ? Math.min(hi, Math.max(lo, v)) : null; };
    const n = num("n", 4, 16); if (n != null) state.n = Math.round(n);
    const s = num("s", 1, 9999); if (s != null) state.seed = Math.round(s);
    const p = num("p", PRICE.min, PRICE.max); if (p != null) state.p = p;
    if (q.has("x")) state.extra = q.get("x").split(",").map(Number)
      .filter((v) => Number.isFinite(v) && v >= PRICE.min && v <= PRICE.max).slice(0, 12);
    $("#n").value = state.n; $("#p").value = state.p;
  }
  let shareTimer = null;
  function writeShare() {
    clearTimeout(shareTimer);
    shareTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      const q = new URLSearchParams();
      if (state.n !== DEFAULT.n) q.set("n", state.n);
      if (state.seed !== DEFAULT.seed) q.set("s", state.seed);
      if (state.p !== DEFAULT.p) q.set("p", state.p.toFixed(2));
      if (state.extra.length) q.set("x", state.extra.map((v) => v.toFixed(3)).join(","));
      const qs = q.toString();
      history.replaceState(null, "", (qs ? `${location.pathname}?${qs}` : location.pathname) + location.hash);
    }, 150);
  }

  function render() { drawChart(); drawStrip(); readouts(); labels(); writeShare(); }
  function update() { recompute(); render(); }

  $("#n").addEventListener("input", (e) => { state.n = Number(e.target.value); state.extra = []; update(); });
  $("#p").addEventListener("input", (e) => { state.p = Number(e.target.value); render(); });
  $("#add").addEventListener("click", () => {
    if (state.extra.length >= 12) return;
    const p = nextRun(ev);
    if (p != null) { state.extra = [...state.extra, p]; update(); }
  });
  $("#resample").addEventListener("click", () => { state.seed += 1; state.extra = []; update(); });
  $("#reset").addEventListener("click", () => {
    Object.assign(state, DEFAULT, { extra: [] });
    $("#n").value = state.n; $("#p").value = state.p;
    update();
  });
  $("#share").addEventListener("click", async (e) => {
    const b = e.currentTarget, said = b.textContent;
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(location.href); b.textContent = "Copied"; }
    catch { b.textContent = "Copy failed"; }
    setTimeout(() => { b.textContent = said; }, 1600);
  });

  readShare();
  update();
</script>
